  "worked_solution": "The height (or altitude) corresponding to $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is a line segment that \n\n- runs from the opposite vertex $R$ to the line $\\overset{⟷}{PQ},$ and\n\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{PQ}.$\n\nTo draw the height, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Extend the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14247051/assets/265ee40283911b754264224b3b0f349b24cae377373941304865b336a53c7b8e.png)\n\n- Draw the perpendicular from $R$ to $\\overset{⟷}{PQ}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14247051/assets/2e48106e4aedb44faef00060f6af9632bd0c8e62eb8d06f12606c2a476bacac3.png)",
